From: The gVisor Authors <gvisor-dev@googlegroups.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:45:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kk: cap maxViewportDimensions to 16384

In src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c, kk_get_device_properties
reports maxViewportDimensions as {32768, 32768} while
maxFramebufferWidth is 16384. Draws with a viewport of 28672 or larger
produce no pixels on Apple Silicon.

Report maxViewportDimensions as {16384, 16384} and viewportBoundsRange
as {-32768, 32767} to match the framebuffer limit and the Vulkan bounds
rule.

License: MIT
---
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
index 65b99ed..05afb6c 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
@@ -618,8 +618,8 @@ kk_get_device_properties(
       .maxSamplerLodBias = 15,
       .maxSamplerAnisotropy = 16,
       .maxViewports = KK_MAX_VIEWPORTS,
-      .maxViewportDimensions = {32768, 32768},
-      .viewportBoundsRange = {-65536, 65536},
+      .maxViewportDimensions = {16384, 16384},
+      .viewportBoundsRange = {-32768, 32767},
       .viewportSubPixelBits = 8,
       .minMemoryMapAlignment = os_page_size,
       .minTexelBufferOffsetAlignment = KK_MIN_TEXEL_BUFFER_ALIGNMENT,
